        <item>
            <title>0.2.5</title>
            <pubDate>Sat, 26 Sep 2026 14:11:51 -0700</pubDate>
            <link>https://nfarina.github.io/brushy</link>
            <sparkle:fullReleaseNotesLink>https://github.com/nfarina/brushy/releases/tag/v0.2.5</sparkle:fullReleaseNotesLink>
            <sparkle:version>7</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.2.5</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
            <description sparkle:format="markdown"><![CDATA[## What's new

- Number keys set the selected layer's opacity, as in Photoshop: 1–9 for 10–90%, 0 for 100%. Type two digits quickly for an exact value (4 then 5 gives 45%, 0 then 0 gives 0%). With a group selected they set the group's opacity, and with the brush or eraser they set the brush opacity.
]]></description>
            <enclosure url="https://github.com/nfarina/brushy/releases/download/v0.2.5/Brushy-macos.zip" length="5756386" type="application/octet-stream" sparkle:edSignature="a9pGeVfv1Z5+vbQPSy5TbzLXAwbHhGhsoJRrc4x7lS3xQ9ecMy7/XWvueWOctig66ggJe3ZqLassKKz1A1KwCg=="/>
        </item>
        <item>
            <title>0.2.4</title>
            <pubDate>Tue, 22 Sep 2026 12:54:57 -0700</pubDate>
            <link>https://nfarina.github.io/brushy</link>
            <sparkle:fullReleaseNotesLink>https://github.com/nfarina/brushy/releases/tag/v0.2.4</sparkle:fullReleaseNotesLink>
            <sparkle:version>6</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.2.4</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
            <description sparkle:format="markdown"><![CDATA[## What's new

- Marquee: a W × H readout in pixels follows the pointer while you drag out a rectangle, as in Photoshop.
- Marquee, lasso and magic wand: the options bar shows the selection's size in pixels, next to the canvas size.
]]></description>
